title: Investment Journey Simulator
message: >-
  If you use this software, or a figure it produced, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dash
    given-names: Sambit Supriya
    alias: sambitd0
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/sambitd0/investment-journey-simulator
abstract: >-
  A long-term investment planning simulator built around one
  question: not what a monthly contribution becomes, but how much
  the decisions along the way change that number. Plans are built
  as timelines of events - start, pause, resume, step up, withdraw,
  close, reopen - and the difference between any two plans is
  attributed to its causes by Shapley value, so the parts sum to
  the whole gap exactly. Lot-level accounting carries Indian
  capital gains treatment, including the short and long term
  boundary, the annual exemption, surcharge with marginal relief
  and grandfathering. The engine is cross-checked against two
  independently written simulators over tens of thousands of
  randomly generated plans.
